{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:two-unit-normals","title":"lem:two-unit-normals","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1814,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:two-unit-normals","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:two-unit-normals","line":2962,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[A Hypersurface Has Exactly Two Unit Normals at Each Point]\n\\label{lem:two-unit-normals}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal, lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame, def:metric-preserving}\n\n\n\n\nIf the normal space at $x$ is the line spanned by a unit normal $w_0$, every unit normal at $x$ is $w_0$ or $-w_0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal}\n\\sketch Write $w=cw_0$. The unit equations give $1=\\langle w,w\\rangle=c^2\\langle w_0,w_0\\rangle=c^2$, hence $c=\\pm1$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[A Hypersurface Has Exactly Two Unit Normals at Each Point] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a74776f2d756e69742d6e6f726d616c73\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal\">↗ def:unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-space-orthonormal-frame\">↗ lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ametric-preserving\">↗ def:metric-preserving</a> <p></p>If the normal space at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> is the line spanned by a unit normal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w_0$\">$w_0$</span>, every unit normal at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w_0$\">$w_0$</span> or <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$-w_0$\">$-w_0$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal\">↗ def:unit-normal</a> \\sketch Write <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w=cw_0$\">$w=cw_0$</span>. The unit equations give <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1=\\langle w,w\\rangle =c^2\\langle w_0,w_0\\rangle =c^2$\">$1=\\langle w,w\\rangle =c^2\\langle w_0,w_0\\rangle =c^2$</span>, hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c=\\pm 1$\">$c=\\pm 1$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-if","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pointwise-unit-normal-span","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal","title":"def:unit-normal","label":"def:unit-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","label":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","label":"def:metric-preserving"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","title":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","label":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:two-unit-normals","title":"lem:two-unit-normals","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[A Hypersurface Has Exactly Two Unit Normals at Each Point]\n\\label{lem:two-unit-normals}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal, lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame, def:metric-preserving}\n\n\n\n\nIf the normal space at $x$ is the line spanned by a unit normal $w_0$, every unit normal at $x$ is $w_0$ or $-w_0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal}\n\\sketch Write $w=cw_0$. The unit equations give $1=\\langle w,w\\rangle=c^2\\langle w_0,w_0\\rangle=c^2$, hence $c=\\pm1$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal","title":"def:unit-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:metric-preserving","title":"def:metric-preserving","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}